            <div xml:id="d805">

                <pb facs="1121" n="993" sameAs="frus:frus1928v01/pg993"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.632/42: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Austria</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Washburn</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vienna</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-05-09T10:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 9, 1928—10
                                a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 1:40 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>23. Department’s telegram 25, April 27, 3 p.m.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Article 11 revised pursuant to Department’s telegram 24, April 26 [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">12</hi>], 6 p.m., and instruction No. 676, April
                            25th.<anchor n="99" xml:id="d805-f1"/></item>
                    <pb facs="1122" n="994" xml:id="pg994"/>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Schüller expressed finally preference for six-year term because of
                        uncertainty of date of Senate ratification. To this I assented in view of
                        paragraph three, Department’s telegram 25.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>Cabinet council is taking necessary formalities and treaty will shortly be
                        signed probably this month in conformity with instruction No. 573, April 14,
                            1927.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d805-f2"/></item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washburn</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
